# [Plan-Step] Brief description (50 chars max)
#
# Detailed explanation (wrap at 72 characters):
# - What changed and why
# - What problem this solves
# - Any important context
#
# Plan: .github/ai-context/plans/002-component-architecture-refactor.md
# Step: [X.Y] [Status: Complete/In Progress/Blocked]
# Phase: [Phase name]
# Architecture: [No changes / See component-system-design.md / Updated X]
#
# Verification:
# - [ ] Code runs without errors
# - [ ] Follows architecture guidelines  
# - [ ] Tests pass (manual testing completed)
# - [ ] Documentation updated
#
# Breaking Changes: [Yes/No - describe if yes]
# Fixes: [Issue number if applicable]
# Co-authored-by: [Name if pair programming]
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Commit Message Format:
#
# Line 1: Type and brief description (50 chars)
# Types: feat, fix, docs, refactor, test, chore
#
# Body: Detailed explanation (72 char wrap)
# - Use bullet points
# - Explain why, not just what
# - Reference plan steps
#
# Footer: Metadata and checklists
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Example:
#
# [2.3] feat: Migrate Enemy to Entity-Component system
#
# Refactored Enemy class to extend Entity instead of GameObject.
# Added Transform, Sprite, Collider, and Physics components.
# Removed duplicate physics code - now handled by Physics component.
# Patrol AI logic remains in Enemy class.
#
# Plan: .github/ai-context/plans/002-component-architecture-refactor.md
# Step: 2.3 [Status: Complete]
# Phase: Component System
# Architecture: See component-system-design.md
#
# Verification:
# - [x] Code runs without errors
# - [x] Follows architecture guidelines
# - [x] Tests pass (Enemy patrols correctly)
# - [x] Documentation updated
#
# Breaking Changes: No
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
